<title>USA: Sappi Ltd-U.S. unions reach tentative settlement.</title>
<headline>Sappi Ltd-U.S. unions reach tentative settlement.</headline>
<dateline>WATERVILLE, Maine 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A unit of Sappi Ltd has tentatively agreed to drop a $38 million lawsuit that alleged workers with sabotaging its Somerset Mill, union and company officials said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Union officials claimed victory and said the company, S.D. Warren, admitted it did not have evidence to support the accusations, which were made in January during prolonged contract negotiations.</p>
<p>&quot;We're pleased that S.D. Warren has realized the error of its ways,&quot; Jeffrey Young, an attorney for the International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers (IAMAW) told reporters.</p>
<p>The IAMAW and United Paper Workers International Unions said in return for the company agreement to end its lawsuit they had agreed to drop a countersuit that sought damages for defamation.</p>
<p>((--Boston bureau, 617-367-4106))</p>
